.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-egress-relay - Manage the on-node SOCKS5 egress relay (citadel #787)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel egress-relay [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
The egress relay lets ANOTHER citadel node on the AceTeam Network tunnel
outbound traffic through THIS node's own network egress -- the server-side
counterpart to 'citadel socks' (which dials OUT through a node from this
machine). It is default OFF and, even when on, only serves a same-org
verified mesh peer: there is no token or passcode fallback.

.PP
Changes here take effect on the next 'citadel work' start (the relay listener
is started once at worker startup, not re-evaluated live). To run a node as a
PURE egress relay -- no worker, no Redis job source -- use 'citadel egress-relay
serve' instead (citadel #1033).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for egress-relay


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-egress-relay-allow-lan(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-egress-relay-disable(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-egress-relay-enable(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-egress-relay-serve(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-egress-relay-status(1)\fP
